<mxfile host="app.diagrams.net"><diagram name="Data Model" id="ott-data"><mxGraphModel dx="1900" dy="1400" grid="1" gridSize="10" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1900" pageHeight="1400" background="#ffffff"><root><mxCell id="0"/><mxCell id="1" parent="0"/>
<mxCell id="t" value="OTT PLATFORM - Data Model (MySQL ACID + MongoDB Flexible Schema + Cassandra Time-Series + Redis Cache)" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;fontSize=20;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#1a237e" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="20" width="1780" height="35" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

<mxCell id="mysqlTitle" value="MYSQL SCHEMAS (Users, Payments, Watchlist - ACID Transactions)" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=#7b1fa2;fillColor=#f3e5f5;align=left;fontSize=14;fontStyle=1;rounded=1" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="80" width="850" height="30" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

<mxCell id="usersTable" value="users table (authentication + subscription)&#10;&#10;PRIMARY KEY: user_id&#10;UNIQUE INDEX: email&#10;&#10;┌──────────────────────┬─────────────────┬────────────────────────────┐&#10;│ Column               │ Type            │ Description                │&#10;├──────────────────────┼─────────────────┼────────────────────────────┤&#10;│ user_id              │ UUID            │ PK, unique identifier      │&#10;│ name                 │ VARCHAR(100)    │ Full name                  │&#10;│ email                │ VARCHAR(255)    │ UNIQUE, login credential   │&#10;│ password_hash        │ VARCHAR(255)    │ bcrypt hashed              │&#10;│ country_code         │ CHAR(2)         │ IN, US, GB for geo content │&#10;│ subscription_status  │ ENUM            │ ACTIVE, EXPIRED, CANCELLED │&#10;│ subscription_plan_id │ UUID            │ FK → subscription_plans    │&#10;│ subscription_expiry  │ DATE            │ 2026-08-21, check on play  │&#10;│ created_at           │ TIMESTAMP       │ Account creation time      │&#10;│ updated_at           │ TIMESTAMP       │ Last modification          │&#10;└──────────────────────┴─────────────────┴────────────────────────────┘&#10;&#10;WHY MySQL for users: Payment subscription requires ACID. If payment succeeds but subscription_status update fails halfway → user charged but no access. MySQL transaction ensures all-or-nothing." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f3e5f5;strokeColor=#7b1fa2;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontFamily=Courier New" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="120" width="850" height="280" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

<mxCell id="plansTable" value="subscription_plans table (plan tiers)&#10;&#10;PRIMARY KEY: plan_id&#10;&#10;┌──────────────────┬─────────────────┬────────────────────────────────┐&#10;│ Column           │ Type            │ Description                    │&#10;├──────────────────┼─────────────────┼────────────────────────────────┤&#10;│ plan_id          │ UUID            │ PK                             │&#10;│ name             │ VARCHAR(50)     │ Basic, Standard, Premium       │&#10;│ price            │ DECIMAL(10,2)   │ 149.00, 499.00, 649.00 INR     │&#10;│ currency         │ CHAR(3)         │ INR, USD, GBP                  │&#10;│ validity_days    │ INT             │ 30 (monthly) or 365 (yearly)   │&#10;│ max_streams      │ INT             │ Basic=1, Standard=2, Premium=4 │&#10;│ max_resolution   │ VARCHAR(10)     │ HD, FHD, UHD (4K)              │&#10;└──────────────────┴─────────────────┴────────────────────────────────┘" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f3e5f5;strokeColor=#7b1fa2;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontFamily=Courier New" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="420" width="850" height="200" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

<mxCell id="paymentsTable" value="payments table (transaction log)&#10;&#10;PRIMARY KEY: payment_id&#10;INDEX: (user_id, paid_at DESC)&#10;&#10;┌──────────────────┬─────────────────┬────────────────────────────────┐&#10;│ Column           │ Type            │ Description                    │&#10;├──────────────────┼─────────────────┼────────────────────────────────┤&#10;│ payment_id       │ UUID            │ PK                             │&#10;│ user_id          │ UUID            │ FK → users.user_id             │&#10;│ amount           │ DECIMAL(10,2)   │ 499.00                         │&#10;│ currency         │ CHAR(3)         │ INR, USD                       │&#10;│ status           │ ENUM            │ SUCCESS, FAILED, REFUNDED      │&#10;│ gateway_txn_id   │ VARCHAR(100)    │ Stripe charge ID ch_xxx        │&#10;│ plan_id          │ UUID            │ FK → subscription_plans        │&#10;│ paid_at          │ TIMESTAMP       │ Transaction timestamp          │&#10;└──────────────────┴─────────────────┴────────────────────────────────┘&#10;&#10;WHY transaction log: Audit trail. If dispute arises, we have gateway_txn_id to cross-reference with Stripe." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f3e5f5;strokeColor=#7b1fa2;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontFamily=Courier New" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="640" width="850" height="240" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

<mxCell id="mongoTitle" value="MONGODB DOCUMENTS (Video Metadata - Flexible Schema for Movies vs Series)" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=#7b1fa2;fillColor=#f3e5f5;align=left;fontSize=14;fontStyle=1;rounded=1" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="970" y="80" width="870" height="30" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

<mxCell id="mongoMovie" value="Movie document (simple structure)&#10;&#10;{&#10;  _id: 'vid-abc',&#10;  type: 'MOVIE',&#10;  title: 'Extraction 2',&#10;  description: 'Tyler Rake is back...',&#10;  genre: ['action', 'thriller'],&#10;  cast: ['Chris Hemsworth', 'Golshifteh Farahani'],&#10;  director: 'Sam Hargrave',&#10;  duration: 7380,                    // seconds&#10;  releaseYear: 2023,&#10;  maturity: '18+',&#10;  country: ['IN', 'US', 'GB'],       // geo availability&#10;  thumbnail: 'https://cdn.../thumb.jpg',&#10;  backdrop: 'https://cdn.../backdrop.jpg',&#10;  manifestHls: 's3://ott-encoded/vid-abc/hls.m3u8',   // ← Apple/iOS requires HLS&#10;  manifestDash: 's3://ott-encoded/vid-abc/dash.mpd',  // ← used everywhere else&#10;  drmKeyId: 'drm-key-abc',&#10;  status: 'PUBLISHED',               // PROCESSING | PUBLISHED | UNPUBLISHED&#10;  createdAt: ISODate('2023-08-01'),&#10;  publishedAt: ISODate('2023-08-15')&#10;}" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f3e5f5;strokeColor=#7b1fa2;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontFamily=Courier New" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="970" y="120" width="870" height="290" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

<mxCell id="mongoSeries" value="Series document (nested structure - DIFFERENT SCHEMA from Movie)&#10;&#10;{&#10;  _id: 'vid-series-xyz',&#10;  type: 'SERIES',&#10;  title: 'Stranger Things',&#10;  description: 'A group of kids in Hawkins...',&#10;  genre: ['sci-fi', 'horror'],&#10;  cast: ['Millie Bobby Brown', 'Finn Wolfhard'],&#10;  creators: ['The Duffer Brothers'],&#10;  maturity: '16+',&#10;  seasons: [&#10;    {&#10;      seasonNumber: 1,&#10;      episodes: [&#10;        {&#10;          episodeId: 'ep-001',&#10;          title: 'Chapter One: The Vanishing of Will Byers',&#10;          duration: 2940,        // 49 minutes&#10;          manifestHls: 's3://ott-encoded/vid-series-xyz/s1e1/hls.m3u8',&#10;          manifestDash: 's3://ott-encoded/vid-series-xyz/s1e1/dash.mpd',&#10;          thumbnail: 'https://cdn.../s1e1_thumb.jpg',&#10;          releaseDate: ISODate('2016-07-15')&#10;        },&#10;        { episodeId: 'ep-002', ... },&#10;        ...&#10;      ]&#10;    },&#10;    { seasonNumber: 2, episodes: [...] },&#10;    ...&#10;  ],&#10;  status: 'PUBLISHED',&#10;  createdAt: ISODate('2016-06-01')&#10;}&#10;&#10;WHY MongoDB flexible schema: Movie has {duration, director}. Series has {seasons: [{episodes: []}]}. MySQL would need 5+ joined tables (series, seasons, episodes, foreign keys). Slow at reads. MongoDB stores one self-contained JSON document — single-query fetch." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f3e5f5;strokeColor=#7b1fa2;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontFamily=Courier New" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="970" y="430" width="870" height="450" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

<mxCell id="cassandraTitle" value="CASSANDRA SCHEMAS (Watch Progress - Time-Series 500K Writes/Sec)" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=#7b1fa2;fillColor=#f3e5f5;align=left;fontSize=14;fontStyle=1;rounded=1" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="920" width="850" height="30" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

<mxCell id="cassandraTable" value="watch_progress table (time-series heartbeat updates)&#10;&#10;PRIMARY KEY: ((profile_id), last_watched)   -- profile_id partition, last_watched clustering&#10;CLUSTERING ORDER: last_watched DESC&#10;TTL: 90 days (auto-expire old data)&#10;&#10;┌──────────────────┬─────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────┐&#10;│ Column           │ Type            │ Description                            │&#10;├──────────────────┼─────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────┤&#10;│ profile_id       │ UUID            │ Partition key (all progress for 1 user)│&#10;│ last_watched     │ TIMESTAMP       │ Clustering key (2026-08-21 22:15:00, sorts rows)│&#10;│ video_id         │ UUID            │ Regular column (which video)           │&#10;│ position_seconds │ INT             │ Resume point (1234 seconds = 20:34)    │&#10;│ duration_seconds │ INT             │ Total video length                     │&#10;│ percent_done     │ FLOAT           │ 17.1% (for UI progress bar)            │&#10;└──────────────────┴─────────────────┴────────────────────────────────────────┘&#10;&#10;Write pattern: UPDATE watch_progress SET position_seconds=1264, last_watched=now() WHERE profile_id=X AND video_id=Y&#10;  → 15M concurrent streams × heartbeat every 30s = 500,000 writes/sec&#10;  → MySQL dies at 50K writes/sec. Cassandra scales linearly.&#10;&#10;Read pattern: SELECT * FROM watch_progress WHERE profile_id=X ORDER BY last_watched DESC LIMIT 20&#10;  → Single-partition read (all data for profile_id=X on one node), ordered by the clustering key. Fast.&#10;  → Powers 'Continue Watching' row on home screen.&#10;&#10;WHY partition key = profile_id, clustering key = last_watched (not video_id): Cassandra can only ORDER BY clustering key columns. Since 'Continue Watching' needs rows sorted by recency, last_watched must be the clustering key; video_id becomes a regular column instead. All watch progress for one user stays co-located on one Cassandra node → single-partition query fast. Alternative: partition by video_id → reading one user's progress requires querying all partitions (scatter-gather), slow." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f3e5f5;strokeColor=#7b1fa2;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontFamily=Courier New" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="960" width="850" height="380" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

<mxCell id="redisTitle" value="REDIS KEY SPACE (Sub-Millisecond Cache + Atomic Counters)" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=#f57f17;fillColor=#fff9c4;align=left;fontSize=14;fontStyle=1;rounded=1" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="970" y="920" width="870" height="30" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

<mxCell id="redisManifest" value="manifest_url:{video_id} (String with TTL) — Manifest Cache&#10;&#10;Key pattern: manifest_url:{video_id}&#10;Value: JSON {manifestHls, manifestDash} S3/CloudFront URLs&#10;TTL: 1 hour (3600 seconds)&#10;&#10;Usage:&#10;  On play start: GET manifest_url:vid-abc&#10;  If exists: return immediately (1ms cache hit)&#10;  If nil: query MongoDB, cache result (SET manifest_url:vid-abc '{...}' EX 3600)&#10;&#10;Example:&#10;  manifest_url:vid-abc  →  '{manifestHls: s3://ott-encoded/vid-abc/hls.m3u8, manifestDash: s3://ott-encoded/vid-abc/dash.mpd}'  (TTL: 3421s)&#10;&#10;WHY cache manifest URL: Play Service hits MongoDB for every play request. 15M concurrent streams start at different times → peak 50K play requests/sec. MongoDB (even sharded) struggles at 50K reads/sec with 5ms latency. Redis cache brings this to 0.1ms. Cache hit 99% → only 500 MongoDB reads/sec. Without Redis: MongoDB becomes bottleneck." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff9c4;strokeColor=#f57f17;strokeWidth=3;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontFamily=Courier New" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="970" y="960" width="870" height="240" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

<mxCell id="redisStreams" value="active_streams:{user_id} (Integer) — Concurrent Stream Counter&#10;&#10;Key pattern: active_streams:{user_id}&#10;Value: Integer count (1, 2, 3, 4...)&#10;TTL: None (manual DECR on stream stop)&#10;&#10;Usage:&#10;  On play start:  count = INCR active_streams:user-123&#10;                  if count exceeds plan.maxStreams → reject with 429 Too Many Streams&#10;  On play stop:   DECR active_streams:user-123&#10;&#10;Example:&#10;  User on Premium plan (max 4 streams):&#10;    INCR active_streams:user-123  →  1  (OK, allow)&#10;    INCR active_streams:user-123  →  2  (OK, allow)&#10;    INCR active_streams:user-123  →  3  (OK, allow)&#10;    INCR active_streams:user-123  →  4  (OK, allow)&#10;    INCR active_streams:user-123  →  5  (REJECT: 429 Too Many Streams, you are on Premium plan which allows max 4)&#10;&#10;WHY atomic INCR: Two clients start streams at exact same millisecond. Without atomic operations, both read count=0, both write count=1 → user exceeds limit undetected. Redis INCR is atomic — Redis serializes the operations, one gets count=1, the other gets count=2." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff9c4;strokeColor=#f57f17;strokeWidth=3;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontFamily=Courier New" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="970" y="1220" width="870" height="280" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

</root></mxGraphModel></diagram></mxfile>
